      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On October 1, we launched our prototype satellite for Project Suncatcher.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:33.792Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The launch marked the first step in our long-term research moonshot to explore powering AI compute in space.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:33.792Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Since then, we've spent the last few weeks completing our commissioning checklist, which included powering up the host and TPU trays and successfully running early machine learning tests.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:33.792Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This week, we reached our \"Hello World\" milestone: the first-ever AI response from a data center class TPU in orbit.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:33.792Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "During a ground-station pass, we uplinked our first prompt to our onboard Gemma 4 open model, asking it to generate a haiku about being in space.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-31T01:33:33.792Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Verifying our TPUs can reliably execute workloads in space paves the way for our next milestone of twin interconnected satellites in 2027.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z",
